## Plain-language summary

You may download, compile, install, run, and privately modify A.R.K.A. for personal and other non-commercial purposes.

Non-commercial study, teaching, academic research, charitable work, volunteer work, evaluation, and informal study groups are allowed. Receiving a salary or stipend does not by itself make those activities commercial.

You may fork A.R.K.A. and publish changes through that fork when preparing and submitting a contribution to the official A.R.K.A. repository.

You may not use A.R.K.A. commercially, include it in a commercial product or service, or distribute a modified version as an independent project without separate written permission.

This summary is for convenience. The terms below govern use of the Software.

