**Software** means A.R.K.A., including its source code, compiled binaries, installers, documentation, assets, and accompanying files, excluding separately licensed third-party components.

**Copyright Holder** means Dongan Yu or a successor who legally owns the relevant copyright in the Software.

**Official Repository** means the official A.R.K.A. repository at https://github.com/DongAnYu/ARKA or a replacement repository identified by the Copyright Holder.

**Commercial Use** means use primarily intended for commercial advantage, revenue generation, monetary compensation from the Software itself, business operations, professional services, or the development, provision, marketing, or support of a product or service.

## 2. Non-Commercial Use Grant

Subject to this Licence, the Copyright Holder grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and non-sublicensable licence to:

1. view, download, and copy the Software;
2. compile, install, and run the Software on any device You own, control, or are authorised to use;
3. make private modifications for Your own non-commercial use;
4. use the Software for personal study, learning, teaching, non-commercial academic research, charitable or volunteer activity, evaluation, experimentation, and informal group study; and
5. share unmodified copies for non-commercial purposes, provided that this Licence and all copyright and attribution notices remain included.

These permissions are available to individuals and organisations only for the non-commercial activities listed above. Receiving an ordinary salary, wage, scholarship, or research stipend does not by itself make an otherwise permitted activity Commercial Use.

Each recipient of a shared unmodified copy receives their rights directly from the Copyright Holder under this Licence. You may not charge a licence fee or access fee for the Software.

## 3. Forks and Contributions

You may fork the Official Repository, modify the Software, test and discuss those modifications, and submit them to the Official Repository through a pull request or another contribution process approved by the Copyright Holder.

A contribution fork may remain publicly visible on its repository-hosting platform. You may not present it as an official or independent version of A.R.K.A., or distribute releases, binaries, installers, or packages built from the modified fork.

By intentionally submitting a contribution, You represent that You have the right to submit it and grant the Copyright Holder a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, irrevocable, royalty-free, transferable, and sublicensable licence to use, reproduce, modify, distribute, relicense, and commercially exploit the contribution in any form.

You retain copyright ownership of Your original contribution. To the extent permitted by law, You waive and agree not to assert moral rights that would prevent exercise of the rights granted above.

## 4. No Commercial Use

Without a separate written licence from the Copyright Holder, You may not:

1. sell, rent, license, sublicense, or otherwise monetise the Software;
2. charge for access to the Software;
3. use the Software as part of a commercial product, service, hosted offering, software-as-a-service offering, or paid professional service;
4. use the Software for the internal business operations of a for-profit organisation;
5. repackage, rebrand, or white-label the Software for commercial purposes; or
6. use the Software to develop, operate, or support a competing commercial product or service.

Non-commercial teaching, study, research, charity, and volunteer activity permitted by Section 2 do not become Commercial Use merely because a participant receives a salary, wage, scholarship, or stipend.

Commercial permission exists only through a separate written agreement authorised by the Copyright Holder.

## 5. Modified Versions

You may keep private modifications for permitted non-commercial use and may publish modifications through the contribution workflow in Section 3.

You may not distribute a modified version, independent release, installer, package, mirror, or derivative project outside that contribution workflow without separate written permission.

